<title>CANADA: British Columbia govt said to plan 3,000 job cuts.</title>
<headline>British Columbia govt said to plan 3,000 job cuts.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Columbia plans to cut up to 3,000 jobs from the provincial payroll as part of its effort to trim C$750 million in spending over the next 18 months, local media reported Friday.</p>
<p>Provincial Premier Glen Clark said the figure was in &quot;the ballpark&quot; during a party planning meeting in Prince Rupert, local radio and newspapers reported. A government spokesman was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>The first cuts are likely to be made within a few weeks. British Columbia has been struggling to rein in spending to be able to meet its budget surplus forecast amid falling revenue.</p>
</text>
